The golden rule:
Derive the visual from the essay. Borrow the craft from the catalog. Show the concept, not the keyword. If a viewer who muted the scene doesn't get it, the visual is wrong — replace it.
Beat rhythm: 5-10s per visual, never more than 7s per shot. Contiguous. Every beat covered. Open on something strong. Vary it — don't repeat the same visual type.
